 "notes": "N087. a GOAL of a linear decoder with a rank-k bottleneck on frozen features (dashed = the fine-tuned model's own head .6730); predictions need about 8-12 dimensions. b frozen features with an MLP decoder (fine-tuned = own linear head; rings = the 2 directions): self-supervised features without fine-tuning (.603) are no better than 144 hand-made per-channel image statistics (.607); autoencoders .594-.624; fine-tuning .673. c clustering of 10,137 held-out draw-0 cells against 10 gated cell types (kNN balanced accuracy, chance .10): autoencoders (.342-.346) beat self-supervised features (.306) but equal image statistics (.354) -> they mostly encode brightness/scatter. d ImageStream sandbox (9 markers per cell, rings = 3 held-out donors): registered co-expression error over 36 marker pairs; learned marker priors (fitted on another donor's joint labels) do not reach all-marker training (autoencoder prior lower than single-marker training on all 3 donors, paired t Holm p < .05, but above the pre-registered .21 bar); all-marker training on 1/9 of the cells (same label count) is as good as on all cells -> joint measurement, not label count, gives the co-expression.",
